{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/chunks/C31.md'","aggregated_output":"# C31 — Reviews, Administration inventory, key rotation\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C30.\n\n## Outcome\n\nConfiguration reviews bind tenant, resource and typed name in the core; Administration renders from an inventory with per-tab capabilities; key rotation is a three-stage flow with one-time secret disclosure through the host.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC30; screens/reviews-administration.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Scopes `Review`, `AdminInventory` (every tab mapped to an admitted `ManagementResource`/`GatewayRead`/C13 read and every action to an admitted `ChangeKind`+`ChangeAction`; AIS and AES unavailable with their gate), topic inventory with distinct detector/topic key types; intents `openReview`, `confirmReview{typed}`, `acknowledgeDeployment`; key rotation is the admitted sequence `ApiKeys·Version` → local acknowledgement → `ApiKeys·Delete` with readback; the issued secret uses the existing `RevealSecret`/`ForgetSecret` host path, is never persisted, and is dropped on every review exit including tenant switch and context retirement.\n2. Administration accordion and tables; review surface with diff, impact, typed name, applied panels; rotation panel states 1–4 (screens/reviews-administration.md); rotation reminder as a distinct Inbox item; two labelled timestamps (deployment acknowledged, old key removed) stored once; unknown outcomes shown as unconfirmed with reconciliation.\n3. Playground verdicts profile-aware with detector and topic results independent; applied topic examples classify under the topic.\n4. Fixtures for R2Admin and R2Review.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- Invariants I3, I6, I7 with V2-R03, R06, R07 and V2-T03, T06, T07, T08; V2-R10 (no mutation intent exists for an unavailable product) and V2-T19 (unavailable product renders no inventory and no action).\n- Known gaps 1–3 of DESIGN-V2 §10 closed with tests.\n- `AdminInventory` is generated from screens/administration-inventory.md and V2-T20 checks every (product, tab) disposition and action set (including Gateway keys: Rotate only, no staged rotation); V2-R11 pins the denied (kind, action) pairs including Gateway key Version; V2-T21 proves Red Team target names remain absent.\n- V2-R07 covers failed and unknown issuance and rejected and unknown deletion as named in screens/reviews-administration.md.\n- Live: one topic review apply and read-back against Redtail under the `airs-v2-c25-` prefix with cleanup, inside the owner scope. Key issuance and deletion are not run live in P09 (covered by C09 fixtures and C25 L-rows).\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28, plus the live apply receipt and cleanup ledger.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nNo production destructive tests; stop on uncertain write outcome and record reconciliation.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
