{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/planning/dependencies.md; head -90 docs/planning/parity-matrix.md; rg -n 'C31|V2-[RTN]0[3678]|T09|T20|T21' docs/planning/test-catalogue.md; ls docs/adr\"","aggregated_output":"# Dependency and source gates\n\nArchitecture proposed exact first-slice versions in docs/architecture/qualification.md.\nAs of C01 (2026-10-17) the desktop graph is resolved, locked and compiled on\nthe macOS ARM64 host; the resolved inputs are recorded below. Later SDK\nfamilies and other inputs remain gated at their consuming chunks.\n\n## Source ownership\n\n| Input          | Inspected revision                       | Ownership/use                                           |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|\n| cdot-framework | e3553b27a3d6bf457a2e585c5ae479c7db89a17b | Selective patterns/modules after provenance evaluation  |\n| Desktop v1     | 74754c02b19d87187b6dca81f64550a669b0f841 | Behavioral/contracts reference; preserve checkout       |\n| Academy        | 7f3a28c4082a5bb278bbff5d79fab106c240155a | Shared React source; hosted learning authority          |\n| Native Harness | 9331a5839bc6a763d94dee7584746f58bbbe1181 | Desktop-capable native engine/protocol input            |\n| SDK Phase 3    | ec6230d2a19b9c835c9e4c9487795b38ad538af3 | Accepted scan subset; native/live qualification pending |\n| scm-sdk crate  | crates.io 0.1.0, sha256 6d555d955c3734dd5ee78f7173569bdecd4426095b2ffedc4b77d8f0f2c2e8d9, from 4f65dc48686a3b701ed0585812fcca46859f7e5a | D027 scan input from C02 (scan feature only); 164 package unit tests pass natively; live qualification is C25 |\n| SDK Phase 4    | 32cbcb6d9b04478aeca21e767ed6ddb8949ec7bb | Accepted management/DLP/IAM subset; qualify exact uses  |\n\nDo not consume an active neighboring worktree via an unpinned path and later\nclaim the accepted commit was built. Obtain a clean revision-specific source\nsnapshot/package without secrets or ignored local configuration. Manifest both\nits origin revision and actual source/package hash. A dependency update reopens\nthe affected contract/native/artifact checks and review. Never fabricate SDK\nmethod parity from a similar TypeScript method name.\n\n## C01 resolved inputs\n\nRecorded by C01 and bound to its review. Locks: `Cargo.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`,\n`rust-toolchain.toml`, `docs/architecture/toolchain.json`,\n`docs/architecture/inputs.lock.json`; the controller's dependency fingerprint\nhashes them with the consumed `.inputs/` bytes and tool identities.\n\n| Input | Resolved | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rust toolchain | 1.99.0 (b940084d7 2026-09-28) | Corrected from 1.90.0; proc-macro dylib dyld failure at deployment target 13.0 on macOS 27 (evidence/C01/toolchain-correction.json). Release `strip` removed for the same failure. |\n| Tauri / tauri-build / Tauri CLI / @tauri-apps/api | 2.12.4 / 2.7.3 / 2.12.3 / 2.12.4 | `custom-protocol` added by the Tauri CLI for bundles |\n| ts-rs | 12.0.1 (serde-compat, no-serde-warnings) | Generated declarations committed; `xtask bindings --check` |\n| React / ReactDOM | 19.2.3 | Single instance per consumer (pnpm strict peers) |\n| Tailwind / Vite / Vitest / plugin-react / TypeScript | 4.3.2 / 7.3.6 / 3.2.6 / 5.2.0 / 5.9.3 | Matched to Academy's resolved lock instead of the earlier 4.1.18 / 7.3.0 proposal |\n| Build Node / pnpm | 24.21.0 / 10.6.5 (corepack shim in `.tools/bin`) | Build-only; never shipped |\n| Academy shared presentation | `ai-security-academy` 891f65eef76b53eb87155d0f0f5622228e217a2d on branch `v2/desktop-presentation` (base 7f3a28c4) | Pushed to the Academy origin on 2026-10-17 (owner-approved; main untouched). `xtask fetch-inputs --source <academy clone>` materializes `.inputs/academy` (tree sha256 1c4ce702…); a fresh clone from origin reproduces it (evidence/C01/clean-checkout). |\n\nThird-party notices for the shipped graph are in `docs/architecture/notice-inventory.json`\n(`xtask notices --check`). The Academy package is Academy-owned and recorded by\nits pinned commit, not relicensed.\n\n## Required gates\n\n- **Distribution terms:** G01 records owner-approved v2 source/binary terms,\n  Academy redistribution permission and every framework-derived import's\n  disposition under [distribution.md](distribution.md). No extraction before\n  clearance; C26 verifies notices/terms against exact shipped inventory.\n\n- **Provenance:** evaluate each direct import's actual license/notice and allowed\n  usage. cdot-framework is not blanket MIT and its billing-retention condition\n  cannot be erased by renaming. Prefer independently implemented patterns where\n  direct copying is unsuitable. Academy sharing is owner-directed; establish\n  package ownership and third-party notices rather than inventing a license.\n- **Academy packaging:** React19/Tailwind4/Vite7 are observed in Academy, while\n  the framework uses React18/Tailwind3. Select a compatible pinned desktop stack\n  and one shared presentation source. The existing UI package re-exports app\n  source and is not a ready independently reusable full learner app.\n- **Shared-source changes:** propose the smallest extraction that supports actual\n  web/desktop consumers. Keep Academy web behavior and hosted contracts stable;\n  run both projects' affected tests. Pin the reviewed shared revision/package\n  before completing its consuming desktop chunk.\n- **SDK scan:** ec6230d2's accepted subset supplies synchronous scan. It requires\n  explicit scan credentials; management OAuth is separate. Accepted Linux\n  reports do not establish macOS ARM64 support. Qualify the native compiler/TLS\n  dependencies, runtime integration, scanner contracts, cancellation, sanitized\n  errors, and unknown outcomes in C02–C03.\n- **SDK administration:** 32cbcb6d's accepted Phase4 is a candidate input for\n  C08–C12. Map every actual operation, option, pagination bound, and error to\n  accepted source/tests. SDK family labels are insufficient proof of parity.\n- **SDK later families:** Phase5 Red Team/Model and Phase6 Gateway were developing\n  or pending during inspection. Their exact accepted pins are prerequisites to\n  C13/C16–C18. Do not consume unfinished work or substitute mocks as completion.\n  Stable v2 must qualify the SDK subset it actually uses, including native/live\n  evidence; it need not claim every unrelated SDK method is complete.\n- **Harness:** retain the desktop-capable native engine/protocol after source and\n  package checks. Do not substitute an older canonical checkout or npm launcher.\n  Rebuild/reseal v2 resources to omit Node/managed CLI where proven unnecessary;\n  old v1 resource hashes do not attest the changed v2 bundle. Preserve inference\n  and MCP routing/context/tool restrictions.\n- **Native host:** select pinned Tauri2/Rust/toolchain dependencies compatible\n  with macOS ARM64 and the chosen SDK. Resolve one application-owned async\n  runtime strategy; do not create an independent runtime per request.\n- **Identity:** specify independent v2 bundle/display/data/Keychain identities in\n  G01. Test v1/v2 coexistence, reset, uninstall, import, and rollback. Do not\n  silently reuse a v1 namespace or change the learner's remote account.\n- **Live environment:** identify designated test tenants/accounts, scopes,\n  reversible resources, budgets, and cleanup/readback before C25 execution.\n  Prod configuration discovery is not mutation authorization. Missing access is\n  a real dependency gap; never report skipped tests as passed.\n- **Hosted OAuth registrations:** G01 maps reuse/new-client/redirect/scope needs\n  for Academy device authorization, Harness company SSO and MCP. Responsible\n  Academy/Gateway/IdP operators own authorized staging/configuration changes and\n  deployment. V2 identity alone neither proves a new registration is required\n  nor authorizes production changes. Resolve before the consuming live tests.\n- **Signing:** identify an authorized Developer ID, provisioning/entitlement\n  requirements, notarization access, and a native acceptance host. Access secrets\n  only at use time through approved storage, never committed plan variables.\n\n## Official host references\n\nTauri supports Rust commands and async messages between presentation and host;\nthe selected command/module interface still requires G01 design and review.\n[Calling Rust](https://v2.tauri.app/develop/calling-rust/)\n\nWindow/WebView capability grants require deliberate scoping; renderer grants do\nnot replace Rust's application authority checks.\n[Capabilities](https://v2.tauri.app/security/capabilities/)\n\nDMG distribution and macOS signing are separate from successful compilation.\n[DMG packaging](https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/dmg/),\n[macOS signing/notarization](https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/sign/macos/).\n# Working-v1 parity and release closure\n\nAll v2 rows are **planned**. No v2 source/native/live/artifact result exists yet.\nThe baseline is [feature-baseline.md](feature-baseline.md); do not expand a\npreview/stub into required live behavior without an explicit scope decision.\n\n| Requirement family                     | Owning chunks   | Closure requirement                                                                  |\n|----------------------------------------|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Tenant setup/scan-only/protected state | C02,C03,C08,C23 | Context/capabilities, reviewed endpoint overrides/profile import, verification/reset |\n| Runtime synchronous scan/cases         | C03,C12         | Faithful verdicts, profiles, cancellation and no silent replay                       |\n| Profiles/topics/applications/keys      | C08,C09         | Exact supported reads/writes, review binding, one-time secrets                       |\n| DLP/deployment catalogue               | C08,C10         | Exact supported operation subset and real multipart semantics                        |\n| Sessions/content/search/cache          | C11             | Explicit reveal, protected persistence, bounded completeness                         |\n| Metadata FP/FN reports                 | C11             | Edit/remove/undo/export without suppression side effects                             |\n| Home/Inbox/source observations/charts  | C12,C18         | Runtime and Gateway data, freshness/partial/unknown/attention                        |\n| Five-product Library/specifications    | C12             | Authoring/import/export; only supported Runtime execution                            |\n| Red Team read-only observations        | C13             | Accepted actual reads; no invented live execution                                    |\n| Model/skill read-only observations     | C13             | Accepted actual reads and partial-source disclosure                                  |\n| API Client documents/projects/imports  | C14             | Fresh-input reconciliation, drafts/conflicts/secrets/Git adoption                    |\n| API Client transport/history/catalogue | C15             | Real HTTP/cookies/downloads, scoped auth, no mutation bypass                         |\n| Gateway workspace/config/admin subset  | C16,C17         | Supported scope/options and reviewed multi-step outcomes                             |\n| Gateway inference/logs/telemetry/cost  | C18             | Streaming, route/model selection, operational budgets/limits                         |\n| Harness native run/stream/lifecycle    | C19             | Real Rust engine/protocol, cleanup and no packaged Node runtime                      |\n| Harness identity/protected history     | C20             | Rust SSO/key lifecycle, scope-safe restore/export/delete                             |\n| Harness typed tools/project permission | C21             | Investigation/proposals and enforced existing sandbox restrictions                   |\n| Workspace MCP                          | C22             | Rust auth/grants, exact call approvals and execution evidence                        |\n| Academy identity/account isolation     | C04             | Device OAuth, scope admission, tenant-independent learner identity                   |\n| Academy learner presentation           | C05             | Shared catalog/lessons/checks/sandbox/UI; feature-local gamification                 |\n| Academy Program/exams/certificates     | C06             | Hosted access/timing/grading/award authority and account workflows                   |\n| Academy encrypted offline work         | C07             | Lease/revision/account-aware reading/drafts; explicit submission                     |\n| Reviewed imports/fresh authentication  | C23             | User work, source preservation, restart/rollback; no old approvals                   |\n| Native UX/privacy/measured performance | C01–C24         | Per-chunk checks plus cumulative actual native quality closure                       |\n| Controlled live behavior               | C25             | Designated scope, real outcomes, readback/cleanup, honest gaps                       |\n| Signed installed package/update        | C26             | DMG/notary/Gatekeeper, exact bytes, fresh user, coexistence/rollback                 |\n\n## Required per-workflow ledger\n\nThe [workflow ledger](../architecture/workflows.md) expands these families into\n66 operation/workflow classes. C01 records machine-readable evidence rows and\nconsuming chunks map exact supported operations/options before implementation.\nEvery row needs an ID, baseline source, current classification, responsible chunk,\nexact SDK/shared dependency contract, and independent expectations. Preserve four\nevidence categories separately: source implementation, fixture/contract results,\nnative/live qualification, and final installed-artifact qualification. Record\ndenied/unsupported/partial results honestly rather than collapsing them to pass.\n\nG01/C01 adds a live_requirement (required/not_required with reason) and separate\nready/blocked-by-access status to every row under [live-checks.md](live-checks.md).\nThe owner approves the expanded list before C25. Missing access cannot shrink\nmandatory scope; a reduction requires a recorded owner decision and new review.\nT23 cross-feature offline acceptance applies to local work and pending operations,\nnot just Academy. C24 closes that cumulative matrix.\n\nV2 source completeness alone does not close a row. Each workflow needs applicable\nsuccess and failure assertions, context/authority coverage, native acceptance and\nrequired live/artifact evidence. C25/C26 review the cumulative ledger against\nthe final frozen input set. A required blocked check blocks stable completion.\n\n## Intentional non-goals and retained classifications\n\n- Financial desktop billing/monetization and media-generation infrastructure are\n  excluded. Remote operational cost/limit administration is retained.\n- Exception Patterns remains explicitly synthetic/inert if shown. FP/FN reports\n  do not suppress scans or modify policy.\n- New Red Team execution and dedicated Model Security execution remain outside\n  parity. Their existence in the new SDK does not authorize adding product scope.\n- Academy admin/assessor operations remain web-only. Learner feedback with an\n  administrative namespace is classified by actual authority, not string matching.\n- No browser app, in-app updater, or additional supported OS/architecture is\n  required for first stable v2.\n- Shared Academy appearance replaces the GPUI presentation implementation. Do\n  not infer a pixel clone or identical internal widget/theme catalogue. Preserve\n  theme preference workflows and specify reviewed mappings for imported settings.\n- The generic SCM workbench catalogue does not prove all 193 requests were live\n  tested. Classify its supported execution/admission separately from dedicated\n  workflows and bind its request metadata to a reviewed source snapshot.\n\nManaged scan/identity HTTP deliberately defaults to Direct rather than v1's\nambient system proxy behavior. On mandatory-proxy networks, onboarding/settings\nshows Direct/System/Explicit policy and requires operator selection; a failed\nfirst request must surface proxy setup rather than an unexplained regression.\nGeneric workbench remains System by default. C02/C15 qualify all modes.\n44:- **T09 Native UI:** actual Tauri command path, menus/shortcuts, keyboard-only\n96:- **T20 Performance:** named macOS hardware/OS/workloads, cold/warm startup, idle\n102:- **T21 Controlled live:** designated account/tenant/entitlements and disposable\n0001-native-operation-authority.md\n0002-academy-shared-presentation.md\n0003-native-harness-and-scoped-identity.md\n0004-managed-workbench-admission.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat crates/desktop-core/src/authority/rotation_domain.rs'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat crates/desktop-core/src/authority/rotation_domain.rs'","aggregated_output":"//! Runtime API key rotation (C31, screens/reviews-administration.md, I6, I7):\n//! the admitted sequence additional key (`ApiKeys · Version`) → local\n//! deployment acknowledgement → old key `Delete` with readback. The core owns\n//! the state per tenant (persisted), drives it from the applied change\n//! results it already settles, and raises the reminder as a distinct Inbox\n//! item until the old key is read back absent. Two timestamps are stored\n//! once and labelled distinctly: when the operator acknowledged the\n//! deployment (a local statement) and when the old key was read back gone.\n//! A failed issuance records nothing; an unknown one is a rotation whose key\n//! is not confirmed until the key inventory shows it; a rejected or unknown\n//! removal keeps the reminder and the completion time unset.\n\nuse serde::Serialize;\nuse serde_json::Value;\nuse ts_rs::TS;\n\nuse super::change_domain::Readback;\nuse super::{Data, Refusal, State, StorageHealth};\nuse crate::changes::{ChangeAction, ChangeKind};\nuse crate::context::ContextRef;\nuse crate::features::{KeyRef, Rotation, RotationIssuance, RotationRemoval};\nuse crate::observation::{Fact, InboxDestination, InboxItem, Tone};\nuse crate::runtime::Outcome;\nuse crate::store::StoreError;\nuse crate::tenants::TenantId;\n\n/// Where a rotation stands, as the panel shows it (derived, never stored).\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, TS)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub enum RotationStage {\n    /// The additional key's issuance settled unknown: nothing confirms a key\n    /// exists until the key inventory is read back.\n    IssuanceUnconfirmed,\n    /// Issued; the one-time secret is still held for this context.\n    Issued,\n    /// Issued earlier; the secret is no longer available.\n    Resumed,\n    /// The operator stated the application was updated.\n    Acknowledged,\n    /// The old key's removal settled unknown: reconciled by readback.\n    RemovalUnconfirmed,\n    /// The old key was read back absent.\n    Complete,\n}\n\n/// One rotation as the presentation shows it.\n#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, TS)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct RotationView {\n    pub application: String,\n    pub old_key: KeyRef,\n    pub new_key: Option<KeyRef>,\n    pub stage: RotationStage,\n    /// The change result that issued the key, while this context holds its\n    /// one-time secret (reveal through the host).\n    pub issued_by: Option<String>,\n    pub issued_at: u32,\n    pub deployment_acknowledged_at: Option<u32>,\n    pub old_key_removed_at: Option<u32>,\n    /// Why the last removal was rejected, if it was.\n    pub removal_rejected: Option<String>,\n    /// What the service established is not yet saved on this Mac (storage\n    /// failed); it is retried on every publication (C31).\n    pub unsaved: bool,\n}\n\n/// What a settled change tells the rotation state (built by the change\n/// domain from its record and output).\npub(super) struct SettledChange {\n    pub(super) operation: String,\n    pub(super) kind: ChangeKind,\n    pub(super) action: ChangeAction,\n    pub(super) target: String,\n    /// The draft's item name (the new key a version names).\n    pub(super) new_name: Option<String>,\n    /// The reviewed item's name (the old key of a version) and the\n    /// application the change named.\n    pub(super) source_name: Option<String>,\n    pub(super) application: Option<String>,\n    pub(super) outcome: Outcome,\n    pub(super) failure: Option<String>,\n    pub(super) readback: Option<Readback>,\n    pub(super) current: Option<String>,\n}\n\n/// The Inbox reminder's id for an application's rotation.\npub fn rotation_item_id(application: &str) -> String {\n    format!(\"rotation-{application}\")\n}\n\nfn key_ref(item: &Value) -> Option<KeyRef> {\n    let id = item.get(\"api_key_id\").and_then(Value::as_str)?.to_owned();\n    let name = item\n        .get(\"api_key_name\")\n        .and_then(Value::as_str)\n        .unwrap_or(\"\")\n        .to_owned();\n    Some(KeyRef { id, name })\n}\n\nfn application_of(item: &Value) -> Option<String> {\n    item.get(\"cust_app\")\n        .and_then(Value::as_str)\n        .filter(|s| !s.is_empty())\n        .map(str::to_owned)\n}\n\nimpl State {\n    fn rotations_mut(&mut self, tenant: &TenantId) -> Option<&mut Vec<Rotation>> {\n        self.data\n            .tenants\n            .iter_mut()\n            .find(|t| &t.profile.id == tenant)\n            .map(|t| &mut t.rotations)\n    }\n\n    /// Applies a settled Runtime change to the active tenant's rotations\n    /// (C31): a key version that read back starts one (replacing an earlier\n    /// rotation of the same application), a version that settled unknown\n    /// starts an unconfirmed one, a failed version records nothing; a delete\n    /// of a rotation's old key completes it when read back absent, keeps it\n    /// with the reason when rejected, and marks it unconfirmed when unknown.\n    pub(super) fn rotation_settled(&mut self, tenant: &TenantId, change: SettledChange) {\n        if change.kind != ChangeKind::ApiKeys {\n            return;\n        }\n        let clock = self.clock();\n        let before = self.data.clone();\n        let Some(rotations) = self.rotations_mut(tenant) else {\n            return;\n        };\n        let changed = match change.action {\n            ChangeAction::Version => {\n                let current = change\n                    .current\n                    .as_deref()\n                    .and_then(|c| serde_json::from_str::<Value>(c).ok());\n                let found = change.outcome == Outcome::Completed\n                    && change.failure.is_none()\n                    && change.readback == Some(Readback::Found);\n                let new_key = current.as_ref().and_then(key_ref).filter(|_| found);\n                let application = current\n                    .as_ref()\n                    .and_then(application_of)\n                    .or_else(|| change.application.clone());\n                let sent = matches!(change.outcome, Outcome::Completed | Outcome::Unknown);\n                match (sent, application) {\n                    // Sent: the rotation starts (or restarts). Confirmed only\n                    // when the readback found the key the review named; a\n                    // completed write whose readback did not establish it,\n                    // or an unknown one, is an unconfirmed issuance that only\n                    // a key of that exact name can confirm later.\n                    (true, Some(application)) => {\n                        rotations.retain(|r| r.application != application);\n                        let confirmed = new_key.is_some();\n                        rotations.push(Rotation {\n                            application,\n                            old_key: KeyRef {\n                                id: change.target.clone(),\n                                name: change.source_name.clone().unwrap_or_default(),\n                            },\n                            new_key,\n                            issuance: if confirmed {\n                                RotationIssuance::Confirmed\n                            } else {\n                                RotationIssuance::Unconfirmed\n                            },\n                            issued_by: Some(change.operation.clone()),\n                            pending_name: change.new_name.clone(),\n                            issued_at: clock,\n                            deployment_acknowledged_at: None,\n                            removal: RotationRemoval::Pending,\n                            old_key_removed_at: None,\n                        });\n                        true\n                    }\n                    // Refused or not sent: nothing issued, nothing kept.\n                    _ => false,\n                }\n            }\n            ChangeAction::Delete => {\n                let Some(rotation) = rotations.iter_mut().find(|r| r.old_key.id == change.target)\n                else {\n                    return;\n                };\n                match (change.outcome, change.failure.as_deref(), change.readback) {\n                    (Outcome::Completed, None, Some(Readback::Absent)) => {\n                        rotation.removal = RotationRemoval::Done;\n                        rotation.old_key_removed_at = Some(clock);\n                    }\n                    (Outcome::Completed, None, _) | (Outcome::Unknown, _, _) => {\n                        // Sent, but the key was not read back gone: reconciled\n                        // by a later whole-inventory read; the reminder stays.\n                        rotation.removal = RotationRemoval::Unconfirmed;\n                    }\n                    (_, failure, _) => {\n                        rotation.removal = RotationRemoval::Rejected {\n                            reason: failure.unwrap_or(\"not sent\").to_owned(),\n                        };\n                    }\n                }\n                true\n            }\n            _ => false,\n        };\n        if changed {\n            self.keep_rotation_fact(&before);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// A complete key inventory page settles what rotations could not\n    /// confirm: an unconfirmed issuance is confirmed by a key of the\n    /// application other than the old one; an unconfirmed removal is done\n    /// once the old key is absent from the whole inventory.\n    pub(super) fn rotation_reconcile(&mut self, tenant: &TenantId, items: &[Value], whole: bool) {\n        let clock = self.clock();\n        let before = self.data.clone();\n        let Some(rotations) = self.rotations_mut(tenant) else {\n            return;\n        };\n        let mut changed = false;\n        for rotation in rotations.iter_mut() {\n            // Only the key this attempt named confirms its issuance: a key the\n            // application already had says nothing about it.\n            if rotation.issuance == RotationIssuance::Unconfirmed\n                && let Some(name) = rotation.pending_name.clone()\n            {\n                let found = items.iter().find(|k| {\n                    application_of(k).as_deref() == Some(rotation.application.as_str())\n                        && k.get(\"api_key_name\").and_then(Value::as_str) == Some(name.as_str())\n                        && key_ref(k).is_some_and(|key| key.id != rotation.old_key.id)\n                });\n                if let Some(key) = found.and_then(key_ref) {\n                    rotation.new_key = Some(key);\n                    rotation.issuance = RotationIssuance::Confirmed;\n                    changed = true;\n                }\n            }\n            // Absence is established only by the whole inventory in one read.\n            if rotation.removal == RotationRemoval::Unconfirmed && whole {\n                let present = items\n                    .iter()\n                    .any(|k| key_ref(k).is_some_and(|key| key.id == rotation.old_key.id));\n                if !present {\n                    rotation.removal = RotationRemoval::Done;\n                    rotation.old_key_removed_at = Some(clock);\n                    changed = true;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if changed {\n            self.keep_rotation_fact(&before);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// A detail read walked the whole key inventory without this key: a\n    /// removal that was sent but not read back gone is now established.\n    pub(super) fn rotation_key_absent(&mut self, tenant: &TenantId, id: &str) {\n        let clock = self.clock();\n        let before = self.data.clone();\n        let Some(rotations) = self.rotations_mut(tenant) else {\n            return;\n        };\n        let mut changed = false;\n        for rotation in rotations\n            .iter_mut()\n            .filter(|r| r.old_key.id == id && r.removal == RotationRemoval::Unconfirmed)\n        {\n            rotation.removal = RotationRemoval::Done;\n            rotation.old_key_removed_at = Some(clock);\n            changed = true;\n        }\n        if changed {\n            self.keep_rotation_fact(&before);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// The operator's statement that the application now uses the new key\n    /// (a local fact, timestamped once).\n    pub(super) fn acknowledge_deployment(\n        &mut self,\n        context: &ContextRef,\n        application: &str,\n    ) -> Result<Option<(String, String)>, Refusal> {\n        let tenant = self.check_context(context)?;\n        let clock = self.clock();\n        let rotations = self.rotations_mut(&tenant).ok_or(Refusal::StaleContext)?;\n        let rotation = rotations\n            .iter_mut()\n            .find(|r| r.application == application)\n            .ok_or(Refusal::InvalidInput)?;\n        if rotation.new_key.is_none() || rotation.removal == RotationRemoval::Done {\n            return Err(Refusal::InvalidInput);\n        }\n        if rotation.deployment_acknowledged_at.is_none() {\n            rotation.deployment_acknowledged_at = Some(clock);\n        }\n        // The operator says the application has the key: once this is\n        // recorded, its one-time copy is no longer needed here (I6).\n        Ok(rotation\n            .issued_by\n            .clone()\n            .map(|operation| (operation, rotation.old_key.id.clone())))\n    }\n\n    /// Saves a rotation fact the service established. Unlike an intent's\n    /// save, a failure keeps the fact in memory (it happened remotely and\n    /// must not be forgotten), reports it, and every later publication\n    /// retries the save; nothing remote is replayed.\n    pub(super) fn keep_rotation_fact(&mut self, _before: &Data) {\n        let saved = match self.storage {\n            StorageHealth::Ready => self.store.save(&self.persisted()),\n            _ => Err(StoreError::Unavailable),\n        };\n        match saved {\n            Ok(()) => {\n                self.durability_unconfirmed = false;\n                self.rotation_unsaved = false;\n            }\n            Err(StoreError::Unconfirmed) => {\n                self.durability_unconfirmed = true;\n                self.rotation_unsaved = false;\n            }\n            Err(_) => self.rotation_unsaved = true,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Retries an unsaved rotation fact (each publication; C31).\n    pub(super) fn retry_rotation_save(&mut self) {\n        if self.rotation_unsaved {\n            let data = self.data.clone();\n            self.keep_rotation_fact(&data);\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// The active tenant's rotations as the presentation shows them.\n    pub(super) fn rotations_view(&self) -> Vec<RotationView> {\n        let Some(tenant) = self.data.active.as_ref().and_then(|id| self.tenant(id)) else {\n            return Vec::new();\n        };\n        tenant\n            .rotations\n            .iter()\n            .map(|r| {\n                let secret = r\n                    .issued_by\n                    .as_deref()\n                    .is_some_and(|op| self.issuance_held(op, &r.old_key.id));\n                let stage = match (\n                    &r.removal,\n                    r.deployment_acknowledged_at,\n                    r.new_key.is_some(),\n                ) {\n                    (RotationRemoval::Done, _, _) => RotationStage::Complete,\n                    (RotationRemoval::Unconfirmed, _, _) => RotationStage::RemovalUnconfirmed,\n                    (_, _, false) => RotationStage::IssuanceUnconfirmed,\n                    (_, Some(_), true) => RotationStage::Acknowledged,\n                    (_, None, true) if secret => RotationStage::Issued,\n                    (_, None, true) => RotationStage::Resumed,\n                };\n                RotationView {\n                    application: r.application.clone(),\n                    old_key: r.old_key.clone(),\n                    new_key: r.new_key.clone(),\n                    stage,\n                    // Offered only while the core holds the key and the stage\n                    // is one that may reveal it (issued, or issued but not yet\n                    // confirmed by readback).\n                    issued_by: r.issued_by.clone().filter(|_| {\n                        secret\n                            && matches!(\n                                stage,\n                                RotationStage::Issued | RotationStage::IssuanceUnconfirmed\n                            )\n                    }),\n                    issued_at: r.issued_at,\n                    deployment_acknowledged_at: r.deployment_acknowledged_at,\n                    old_key_removed_at: r.old_key_removed_at,\n                    unsaved: self.rotation_unsaved,\n                    removal_rejected: match &r.removal {\n                        RotationRemoval::Rejected { reason } => Some(reason.clone()),\n                        _ => None,\n                    },\n                }\n            })\n            .collect()\n    }\n\n    /// The reminder items of rotations in progress (I7): one per application\n    /// with a confirmed new key and the old key not yet read back gone.\n    pub(super) fn rotation_items(&self) -> Vec<InboxItem> {\n        let Some(tenant) = self.data.active.as_ref().and_then(|id| self.tenant(id)) else {\n            return Vec::new();\n        };\n        tenant\n            .rotations\n            .iter()\n            .filter(|r| r.new_key.is_some() && r.removal != RotationRemoval::Done)\n            .map(|r| InboxItem {\n                id: rotation_item_id(&r.application),\n                title: format!(\n                    \"Update {} with the new key, then remove the old key\",\n                    r.application\n                ),\n                detail: format!(\n                    \"An additional key was issued for {}. Once the application uses it, finish the rotation by removing the old key {}.\",\n                    r.application, r.old_key.name\n                ),\n                source: \"API keys · rotation\".to_owned(),\n                action: true,\n                tone: Tone::Warn,\n                destination: InboxDestination::ApiKeys,\n                action_label: \"Finish rotation…\".to_owned(),\n                facts: vec![\n                    Fact {\n                        label: \"Application\".to_owned(),\n                        value: r.application.clone(),\n                    },\n                    Fact {\n                        label: \"New key\".to_owned(),\n                        value: r.new_key.as_ref().map(|k| k.name.clone()).unwrap_or_default(),\n                    },\n                    Fact {\n                        label: \"Old key\".to_owned(),\n                        value: r.old_key.name.clone(),\n                    },\n                ],\n                per_mille: None,\n            })\n            .collect()\n    }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
