{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^(##|###).*D0(14|26|34|58|59|60)'\"' docs/planning/decisions.md; cat docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md; cat docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md\"","aggregated_output":"160:## D014 — Rust application authority\n275:## D026 — Codex independent review of every chunk and phase\n507:## D034 — Chunk reviews at 8/10; phase sign-off at 9/10 with every chunk raised\n2391:## D058 — UI v2 \"Refined Native\": frozen prototype, P09 extraction plan\n2451:## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8\n2502:## D060 — No import from the alpha; this desktop is v1\n# Prototype boards → test fixtures\n\nEvery wrapper board on the canvas page \"Refined Native v2\" (version 134) is\na reviewed state. Each becomes a named Vitest fixture with the same initial\nprops, so reviewed-state coverage is auditable from this table without the\ncanvas. Props are the `data-props` of `prototype/R2App.dc.html`\n(`start`, `convo`, `theme`, `overlay`) and `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html`\n(`step`, `filled`, `verify`, `theme`, `mode`).\n\n| Board | Component | Initial props | Fixture id | Primary tests | Chunk |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R2App (default) | R2App | start=home, theme=light | `fx.home` | V2-T09, T10, T11 | C28 |\n| R2Dark | R2App | start=home, theme=dark | `fx.home.dark` | token contrast snapshot | C28 |\n| R2Palette | R2App | start=home, overlay=palette | `fx.palette` | palette filter/dispatch, N03 | C28 |\n| R2Tenants | R2App | start=home, overlay=tenants | `fx.switcher` | V2-T01, T02 | C28/C30 |\n| R2AddTenant | R2Onboard | mode=add, step=tenant | `fx.addTenant` | cancel semantics, no Back on the first step | C29 |\n| R2AddTenant drafted | R2Onboard | mode=add, step=tenant, drafted | `fx.addTenant.drafted` | optional scan key, Continue open | C29 |\n| R2On01 Welcome | R2Onboard | step=welcome | `fx.on.welcome` | copy constants | C29 |\n| R2On02 Tenant | R2Onboard | step=tenant, filled=false | `fx.on.tenant.empty` | validation, aria-invalid | C29 |\n| R2On02b Tenant filled | R2Onboard | step=tenant, filled=true | `fx.on.tenant.filled` | rail context line, continue enabled | C29 |\n| R2On03 Products | R2Onboard | step=products | `fx.on.products` | unavailable products not selectable (P18) | C29 |\n| R2On04 Verify | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=running | `fx.on.verify.running` | streaming order | C29 |\n| R2On04b Verify warning | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=warn | `fx.on.verify.warn` | warning row → Inbox item at completion | C29 |\n| R2On04c Verify fail | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=fail | `fx.on.verify.fail` | fix-and-verify-again path | C29 |\n| R2On04d Verify stale | R2Onboard | step=verify, verify=done, inputs changed | `fx.on.verify.stale` | results no longer count; later steps unreachable | C29 |\n| R2On05 Packs | R2Onboard | step=packs | `fx.on.packs` | pack counts, optional | C29 |\n| R2On06 Academy | R2Onboard | step=academy | `fx.on.academy` | hosted sign-in or skip (P19) | C29 |\n| R2On07 Done | R2Onboard | step=done | `fx.on.done` | finite open, `onboarding=done` | C29 |\n| R2Inbox | R2App | start=inbox | `fx.inbox` | V2-T04, T12, T13 | C30 |\n| R2Fresh | R2App | start=home, tenant never read | `fx.fresh` | first read pending, empty Inbox (I12) | C30 |\n| R2Admin | R2App | start=admin | `fxAdmin` (v2/admin/administration.test.tsx) | V2-T19, T20, per-tab labels | C31 |\n| R2Review | R2App | start=admin, overlay=review | `fxAdmin` + `review()`/`rotation()` (same file) | V2-T03, T06, T08; T07 in `ui_v2_reviews` | C31 |\n| R2Harness | R2App | start=harness, convo=blocks | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-blocks.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17 | C32 |\n| R2Harness2 | R2App | start=harness, convo=mcp | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-mcp.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17 (Gateway MCP read, P16) | C32 |\n| R2Harness3 | R2App | start=harness, convo=keys | `fxHarness` + `harness-lifecycle-keys.json` (v2/harness/harness.test.tsx) | V2-T17, T18 | C32 |\n| R2Api | R2App | start=api | `fxApi` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | V2-T14; V2-R05, T05 in `ui_v2_workbench` | C33 |\n| R2Cases | R2App | start=cases | `fxCases` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | V2-T15, T16 | C33 |\n| Show the calls | R2App, any start (no prototype board) | `fxCalls` (v2/fixtures.ts; v2/workbench/workbench.test.tsx) | panel shown only while chosen, never a secret (P54) | C33 |\n| R2Academy | R2App | start=academy | `fx.academy` | embed mounts, theme | C34 |\n\nTest ids: `V2-Txx` Vitest (desktop app), `V2-Rxx` Rust integration\n(desktop-core), `V2-Nxx` native checks (`native-checks.json`). Registry of\nids: [../invariants.md](../invariants.md) plus the per-screen contracts.\n# Provenance and intentional deviations\n\nEvery fixture file and screen contract cites the frozen prototype file and the\nprototype state names it derives from. This file lists where the\nimplementation deliberately differs from the prototype and why. Anything not\nlisted here is expected to match the prototype's behaviour and spacing.\n\nFrozen reference: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL,\npage \"Refined Native v2\", version 134 (version id 1793059808-4929, published\n2026-10-26). Files and hashes: [prototype/MANIFEST.sha256](prototype/MANIFEST.sha256).\n\n| # | Prototype | Implementation | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P1 | Wizard tenant step draws the scan key, management client secret and Gateway workspace key as text fields (`R2Onboard` `f.scanKey`, `f.secret`, `f.gwKey`) | \"Add scan key…\" button opens the host's native secret sheet; the step then shows a masked indicator and the vault record id | The web layer never holds a secret (D014, C09 reveal ownership). Visual delta: button plus masked state instead of a field |\n| P2 | Rotation panel renders the secret in a readonly input with Reveal/Copy (`R2App` `secretShown`) | Reveal shows the secret in the host secret sheet; Copy goes through the host clipboard; both consume a one-time disclosure token | Invariant I6; same reason as P1 |\n| P3 | State lives in one component with `byTenant` (`R2App` `TS/ts/tPatch`) | Core-owned scopes per [state-ownership.md](state-ownership.md) | D014 authority; prototype state model is normative for invariants only |\n| P4 | ⌘1–⌘9 are advertised but not bound (canvas rule: no global key handlers) | Native menu defines the shortcuts and dispatches `navigate` | Host owns menus; works under VoiceOver and shows in the menu bar |\n| P5 | Sidebar lists Home, Inbox, Harness, Academy, Test Cases, API Client, Administration | Same, backed by Rust feature ids `home`, `inbox`, `harness`, `academy`, `library`, `apiClient`, `administration`; `gateway` and `redTeam` move inside Administration; `sessions`, `import`, `settings` reachable from the palette and Administration | One Rust inventory feeds menu, sidebar and palette |\n| P6 | Wizard boards are 1440×900 with a fixed 320px rail | Minimum window 1180×720; rail collapses to icons below 1280 wide | 13-inch displays |\n| P7 | Toasts expire on timers always | Persist until dismissed under Reduce Motion | Native acceptance Reduce Motion check |\n| P8 | Inbox items, Harness lifecycles, API responses, cases and Academy progress are invented in-component data | Wire fixtures in `packages/desktop-contracts/fixtures/wire`, content derived from the prototype data | Fixtures are the contract test surface; prototype data is never shipped |\n| P9 | `TOPICS.injo` added in round 16 as a separate key from detector `inj` | Core topic inventory keys are a distinct type from detector ids | Carries the round-16 fix into the type system |\n| P10 | Administration creation label is a per-product single value | Per-tab creation capability and label in `AdminInventory` | Round 16 finding: wrong label on API keys, Security profiles and Logs tabs |\n| P11 | Home snooze button hard-codes \"Snooze